{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And who shall endure</b> — doubled, like 'endure your goods' and 'they shall endure.'" "<b>For He is like a refiner's fire</b> — behold, this prophecy is in the prophecy of Zechariah: 'and I will bring the third part through the fire.'" "<b>And like fuller's</b> — lye of launderers."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The lemma reads מכלכל ('endure/sustain'); Ibn Ezra notes it is a doubled root, comparing forms from the root כול/כלל.", 1 "Cross-reference to Zechariah 13:9.", 2 "Hebrew בורית glossed as 'סמוך של מכבסים'; here 'סמוך' likely means the alkali/lye used by fullers, not the Hebrew grammatical term for construct state."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:19.448914181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}